IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa-definitions`

-- coa9-publication.l4: Companies Act 2006 (UK), Part 15 Chapter 7, second half: website publication, the right to demand copies,
-- and the requirements in connection with publication (ss 426B, 427-429 (blank), 430, 431, 432, 433, 434, 435, 436),
-- lines 5707-5841 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: as in coa9-strategic.l4. Sections 427, 428 and 429 are blank in this text, as are s 430(2C), (4ZA), (4A)(c)
-- and (8), s 431(1)(ba), s 434(6) and s 435(7).
--
-- BARS. Where the text bars an act (s 434(2), s 435(2): "must not"), the function is the bar: JUST TRUE means the section bars it,
-- never "the company may". A bar's NOTHING and JUST FALSE are not a permission.
--
-- REGULATIVE RULES. The seven days of s 431(3) and s 432(3) are also written as regulative rules (`s 431(3) the company must comply with
-- the demand`, `s 432(3) ...`), run with #TRACE in coa9-tests-publication.l4. A #TRACE adds no assertion line to the counts check.sh prints,
-- so each duty is also a decision function (`s 431(3) the demand was complied with in time`) whose answers are asserted.

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 426B: Section 172(1) statement to be made available on website
-- =========================================================================================================

§ `s 426B Section 172(1) statement to be made available on website`

-- src:5708 | 426B Section 172(1) statement to be made available on website
-- src:5709 | (1) This section applies if—
-- src:5710 | (a) a company is required by section 414CZA to include a section 172(1) statement in its strategic report for a financial year, and
-- src:5711 | (b) the company is an unquoted company in relation to that financial year.
@ref s 426B(1) The section applies if the company must include a section 172(1) statement and is an unquoted company (src:5708-5711)
GIVEN `s 414CZA(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 385 the company is an unquoted company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 426B(1) this section applies to the company` MEANS
    IF `s 414CZA(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `s 385 the company is an unquoted company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", reading (a) for a lawyer): "This section applies if— (a) a company is required by section 414CZA to include a section 172(1) statement ..., and (b) the company is an unquoted company in relation to that financial year"
    ELSE IF `s 414CZA(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            AND `s 385 the company is an unquoted company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 414CZA(2) or section 385 was not answered

-- src:5712 | (2) The company must ensure that the section 172(1) statement—
-- src:5713 | (a) is made available on a website, and
-- src:5714 | (b) remains so available until—
-- src:5715 | (i) the section 172(1) statement for the company’s next financial year is made available in accordance with this section, or
-- src:5716 | (ii) if the obligation under this section to make a section 172(1) statement available does not arise in relation to the company’s next financial year, the end of the company’s next financial year.
@ref s 426B(2) The company must ensure the statement is available on a website until the next one is available (src:5712-5716)
GIVEN `the date on which the section 172(1) statement for the company's next financial year is made available in accordance with this section` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the obligation under this section to make a section 172(1) statement available does not arise in relation to the company's next financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the end of the company's next financial year` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 426B(2)(b) the last day until which the statement must remain available on a website` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date on which the section 172(1) statement for the company's next financial year is made available in accordance with this section`
    WHEN JUST nextStatement THEN JUST nextStatement -- (i)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the obligation under this section to make a section 172(1) statement available does not arise in relation to the company's next financial year`
        THEN JUST `the end of the company's next financial year` -- (ii)
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): neither (i) nor (ii) has yet happened, so the day is not yet fixed

@ref s 426B(2) (src:5712)
GIVEN `the statement is made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement remains so available until the day in subsection (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 426B(2) the company has ensured that the section 172(1) statement is made available on a website and remains so available` MEANS
    IF `the statement is made available on a website` AND `the statement remains so available until the day in subsection (2)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a bare "must" not met, decided case by case, fork F23): "The company must ensure that the section 172(1) statement— (a) is made available on a website, and (b) remains so available until"

-- src:5717 | (3) The section 172(1) statement must be made available on a website that—
-- src:5718 | (a) is maintained by or on behalf of the company, and
-- src:5719 | (b) identifies the company in question.
@ref s 426B(3) The website must be maintained by or on behalf of the company and identify it (src:5717-5719)
GIVEN `the website is maintained by or on behalf of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the website identifies the company in question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 426B(3) the website meets the requirements of the subsection` MEANS
    IF `the website is maintained by or on behalf of the company` AND `the website identifies the company in question`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a bare "must" not met, decided case by case, fork F23): "The section 172(1) statement must be made available on a website that— (a) is maintained by or on behalf of the company, and (b) identifies the company in question."

-- src:5720 | (4) Access to the section 172(1) statement made available on the website under subsection (2), and the ability to obtain a hard copy of the statement from the website, must not be—
-- src:5721 | (a) conditional on the payment of a fee, or
-- src:5722 | (b) otherwise restricted, except so far as necessary to comply with any enactment or regulatory requirement (in the United Kingdom or elsewhere).
@ref s 426B(4) Access to the statement must not be conditional on a fee or otherwise restricted (src:5720-5722)
GIVEN `access to the statement, or the ability to obtain a hard copy of it from the website, is conditional on the payment of a fee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `access or the ability to obtain a hard copy is otherwise restricted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the restriction is necessary to comply with an enactment or regulatory requirement (in the United Kingdom or elsewhere)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 426B(4) access to the statement meets the requirements of the subsection` MEANS
    IF `access to the statement, or the ability to obtain a hard copy of it from the website, is conditional on the payment of a fee`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be— (a) conditional on the payment of a fee"
    ELSE IF `access or the ability to obtain a hard copy is otherwise restricted` AND NOT (`the restriction is necessary to comply with an enactment or regulatory requirement (in the United Kingdom or elsewhere)`)
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be— ... (b) otherwise restricted, except so far as necessary to comply with any enactment or regulatory requirement"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:5723 | (5) The section 172(1) statement—
-- src:5724 | (a) must be made available on a website as soon as reasonably practicable, and
-- src:5725 | (b) must be kept available throughout the period specified in subsection (2)(b)(i) or (as the case may be) (ii).
@ref s 426B(5) The statement must be made available as soon as reasonably practicable and kept available throughout the period (src:5723-5725)
GIVEN `the statement was made available on a website as soon as reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement was kept available throughout the period specified in subsection (2)(b)(i) or (as the case may be) (ii)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 426B(5) the statement was made available and kept available as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the statement was made available on a website as soon as reasonably practicable`
       AND `the statement was kept available throughout the period specified in subsection (2)(b)(i) or (as the case may be) (ii)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a bare "must" not met, decided case by case, fork F23): "The section 172(1) statement— (a) must be made available on a website as soon as reasonably practicable, and (b) must be kept available throughout the period"

-- src:5726 | (6) A failure to make the section 172(1) statement available on a website throughout the period specified in subsection (2)(b)(i) or (as the case may be) (ii) is disregarded if—
-- src:5727 | (a) the statement is made available on the website for part of that period, and
-- src:5728 | (b) the failure is wholly attributable to circumstances that it would not be reasonable to have expected the company to prevent or avoid.
@ref s 426B(6) A failure that is wholly attributable to circumstances the company could not reasonably have prevented is disregarded (src:5726-5728)
GIVEN `the statement is made available on the website for part of the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure is wholly attributable to circumstances that it would not be reasonable to have expected the company to prevent or avoid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 426B(6) the failure to make the statement available throughout the period is disregarded` MEANS
    IF `the statement is made available on the website for part of the period`
       AND `the failure is wholly attributable to circumstances that it would not be reasonable to have expected the company to prevent or avoid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", reading (a) for a lawyer): "A failure to make the section 172(1) statement available on a website throughout the period specified in subsection (2)(b)(i) or (as the case may be) (ii) is disregarded if— (a) ..., and (b) ..."

-- src:5729 | (7) In the event of default in complying with this section, an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 426B(7) An officer in default commits an offence (src:5729)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 426B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 426B(7) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`default is made in complying with section 426B`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", reading (a) for a lawyer): "In the event of default in complying with this section, an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is decided by section 1121

-- src:5730 | (8) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (7) is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 426B(8) Penalty for an offence under section 426B(7) (src:5730)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 426B(8) the penalty for an offence under section 426B(7)` MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection provides only for liability on summary conviction

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 430: Quoted companies: annual accounts and reports to be made available on website
-- (ss 427, 428 and 429 are blank in this text)
-- =========================================================================================================

§ `s 430 Quoted companies: annual accounts and reports to be made available on website`

-- src:5738 | 430 Quoted companies ...: annual accounts and reports to be made available on website
-- src:5739 | (1) A quoted company ... must ensure that its annual accounts and reports—
-- src:5740 | (a) are made available on a website, and
-- src:5741 | (b) ... remain so available until the annual accounts and reports for the company's next financial year are made available in accordance with this section.
@ref s 430(1) A quoted company must ensure its annual accounts and reports are available on a website until the next ones (src:5738-5741)
GIVEN `s 385 the company is a quoted company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the annual accounts and reports are made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they remain so available until the annual accounts and reports for the company's next financial year are made available in accordance with this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 430(1) the quoted company has ensured that its annual accounts and reports are available on a website` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 385 the company is a quoted company`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a quoted company is decided by section 385
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A quoted company ... must ensure"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (c))
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the annual accounts and reports are made available on a website`
           AND `they remain so available until the annual accounts and reports for the company's next financial year are made available in accordance with this section`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a bare "must" not met, decided case by case, fork F24): "A quoted company ... must ensure that its annual accounts and reports— (a) are made available on a website, and (b) ... remain so available until the annual accounts and reports for the company's next financial year are made available"

-- src:5742 | (2) The annual accounts and reports must be made available on a website that—
-- src:5743 | (a) is maintained by or on behalf of the company, and
-- src:5744 | (b) identifies the company in question.
@ref s 430(2) The website must be maintained by or on behalf of the company and identify it (src:5742-5744)
GIVEN `the website is maintained by or on behalf of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the website identifies the company in question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 430(2) the website meets the requirements of the subsection` MEANS
    IF `the website is maintained by or on behalf of the company` AND `the website identifies the company in question`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a bare "must" not met, decided case by case, fork F24): "The annual accounts and reports must be made available on a website that— (a) is maintained by or on behalf of the company, and (b) identifies the company in question."

-- src:5745 | (2A) If the directors' remuneration policy of a quoted company ... is revised in accordance with section 422A ... the company must ensure that the revised ... policy is made available on the website on which its annual accounts and reports are made available.
@ref s 430(2A) A quoted company must ensure a revised remuneration policy is made available on the website (src:5745)
GIVEN `s 385 the company is a quoted company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the directors' remuneration policy of the company is revised in accordance with section 422A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 430(2A) the quoted company must ensure that the revised policy is made available on the website on which its annual accounts and reports are made available` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 385 the company is a quoted company`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a quoted company is decided by section 385
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the directors' remuneration policy of a quoted company"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (c))
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the directors' remuneration policy of the company is revised in accordance with section 422A`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", reading (a) for a lawyer; fork F33): "If the directors' remuneration policy of a quoted company ... is revised in accordance with section 422A ... the company must ensure"

@ref s 430(2A) A quoted company must ensure a revised remuneration policy is made available on the website (src:5745)
DECLARE `s 430(2B) information about a person who ceases to be a director` IS ONE OF
    `s 430(2B)(a) the name of the person concerned`
    `s 430(2B)(b) particulars of any remuneration payment made or to be made to the person after ceasing to be a director, including its amount and how it was calculated`
    `s 430(2B)(c) particulars of any payment for loss of office made or to be made to the person, including its amount and how it was calculated`

-- src:5746 | (2B) If a person ceases to be a director of a quoted company ..., the company must ensure that the following information is made available on the website on which its annual accounts and reports are made available—
-- src:5747 | (a) the name of the person concerned,
-- src:5748 | (b) particulars of any remuneration payment (within the meaning of Chapter 4A of Part 10) made or to be made to the person after ceasing to be a director, including its amount and how it was calculated, and
-- src:5749 | (c) particulars of any payment for loss of office (within the meaning of that Chapter) made or to be made to the person, including its amount and how it was calculated.
@ref s 430(2B) When a person ceases to be a director of a quoted company, the company must make this information available on the website (src:5746-5749)
GIVEN `s 385 the company is a quoted company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a person ceases to be a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `such a payment has been made or is to be made to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      information IS A `s 430(2B) information about a person who ceases to be a director`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 430(2B) the quoted company must ensure that the information is made available on the website` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 385 the company is a quoted company`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a quoted company is decided by section 385
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a quoted company"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (c))
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF NOT (`a person ceases to be a director of the company`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", reading (a) for a lawyer; fork F33): "If a person ceases to be a director of a quoted company ..., the company must ensure that the following information is made available"
        ELSE CONSIDER information
             WHEN `s 430(2B)(a) the name of the person concerned` THEN JUST TRUE
             OTHERWISE
                 IF `such a payment has been made or is to be made to the person`
                 THEN JUST TRUE
                 ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "particulars of any ... payment ... made or to be made to the person"; where there is no such payment the paragraph names nothing to disclose

-- src:5751 | (3) Access to the material made available on the website under subsections (1) to (2B), and the ability to obtain a hard copy of such material from the website, must not be—
-- src:5752 | (a) conditional on the payment of a fee, or
-- src:5753 | (b) otherwise restricted, except so far as necessary to comply with any enactment or regulatory requirement (in the United Kingdom or elsewhere).
@ref s 430(3) Access to the material must not be conditional on a fee or otherwise restricted (src:5751-5753)
GIVEN `access to the material, or the ability to obtain a hard copy of it from the website, is conditional on the payment of a fee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `access or the ability to obtain a hard copy is otherwise restricted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the restriction is necessary to comply with an enactment or regulatory requirement (in the United Kingdom or elsewhere)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 430(3) access to the material meets the requirements of the subsection` MEANS
    IF `access to the material, or the ability to obtain a hard copy of it from the website, is conditional on the payment of a fee`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be— (a) conditional on the payment of a fee"
    ELSE IF `access or the ability to obtain a hard copy is otherwise restricted` AND NOT (`the restriction is necessary to comply with an enactment or regulatory requirement (in the United Kingdom or elsewhere)`)
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be— ... (b) otherwise restricted, except so far as necessary to comply with any enactment or regulatory requirement"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:5754 | (4) The annual accounts and reports—
-- src:5755 | (a) must be made available as soon as reasonably practicable, and
-- src:5756 | (b) ... must be kept available throughout the period specified in subsection (1)(b).
@ref s 430(4) The annual accounts and reports must be made available as soon as reasonably practicable and kept available (src:5754-5756)
GIVEN `the annual accounts and reports were made available as soon as reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they were kept available throughout the period specified in subsection (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 430(4) the annual accounts and reports were made available and kept available as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the annual accounts and reports were made available as soon as reasonably practicable`
       AND `they were kept available throughout the period specified in subsection (1)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a bare "must" not met, decided case by case, fork F24): "The annual accounts and reports— (a) must be made available as soon as reasonably practicable, and (b) ... must be kept available throughout the period specified in subsection (1)(b)"

-- src:5758 | (4A) Where subsection (2A) or (2B) applies, the material in question—
-- src:5759 | (a) must be made available as soon as reasonably practicable, ... and
-- src:5760 | (b) must be kept available until the next directors' remuneration report of the company is made available on the website. ...
@ref s 430(4A) Material under subsection (2A) or (2B) must be made available promptly and kept available until the next remuneration report is available (src:5758-5760)
GIVEN `subsection (2A) or (2B) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the material was made available as soon as reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the material was kept available until the next directors' remuneration report of the company was made available on the website` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 430(4A) the material was made available and kept available as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF NOT (`subsection (2A) or (2B) applies`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a "where" condition that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b); fork F33): "Where subsection (2A) or (2B) applies"
    ELSE IF `the material was made available as soon as reasonably practicable`
            AND `the material was kept available until the next directors' remuneration report of the company was made available on the website`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a bare "must" not met, decided case by case, fork F24): "the material in question— (a) must be made available as soon as reasonably practicable, ... and (b) must be kept available until the next directors' remuneration report of the company is made available on the website"

-- src:5762 | (5) A failure to make material available on a website throughout the period mentioned in subsection (4) or (as the case may be) ... (4A) is disregarded if—
-- src:5763 | (a) the material is made available on the website for part of that period, and
