      `the failure is wholly attributable to circumstances that it would not be reasonable to have expected the company to prevent or avoid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 430(5) the failure to make material available throughout the period is disregarded` MEANS
    IF `the material is made available on the website for part of the period`
       AND `the failure is wholly attributable to circumstances that it would not be reasonable to have expected the company to prevent or avoid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", reading (a) for a lawyer): "A failure to make material available on a website throughout the period mentioned in subsection (4) or (as the case may be) ... (4A) is disregarded if— (a) ..., and (b) ..."

