-- src:5818 | 435 Requirements in connection with publication of non-statutory accounts
-- src:5819 | (1) If a company publishes non-statutory accounts, it must publish with them a statement indicating—
-- src:5820 | (a) that they are not the company's statutory accounts,
-- src:5821 | (b) whether statutory accounts dealing with any financial year with which the non-statutory accounts purport to deal have been delivered to the registrar, and
-- src:5822 | (c) whether an auditor's report has been made on the company's statutory accounts for any such financial year, and if so whether the report—
-- src:5823 | (i) was qualified or unqualified, or included a reference to any matters to which the auditor drew attention by way of emphasis without qualifying the report, or
-- src:5824 | (ii) contained a statement under section 498(2) (accounting records or returns inadequate or accounts or directors' remuneration report not agreeing with records and returns), or section 498(3) (failure to obtain necessary information and explanations).
@ref s 435(1) A company that publishes non-statutory accounts must publish with them a statement indicating these matters (src:5818-5824)
GIVEN `the company publishes non-statutory accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an auditor's report has been made on the company's statutory accounts for a financial year with which the non-statutory accounts purport to deal` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `s 435(1) matter the statement must indicate`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 435(1) the company must publish with the non-statutory accounts a statement indicating the matter` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company publishes non-statutory accounts`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", reading (a) for a lawyer; fork F33): "If a company publishes non-statutory accounts, it must publish with them a statement indicating"
    ELSE CONSIDER matter
         WHEN `s 435(1)(c)(i) whether the report was qualified or unqualified, or included a reference to any matters to which the auditor drew attention by way of emphasis without qualifying the report` THEN
             IF `an auditor's report has been made on the company's statutory accounts for a financial year with which the non-statutory accounts purport to deal`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", reading (a) for a lawyer; fork F33): "and if so whether the report"
         WHEN `s 435(1)(c)(ii) whether the report contained a statement under section 498(2) or section 498(3)` THEN
             IF `an auditor's report has been made on the company's statutory accounts for a financial year with which the non-statutory accounts purport to deal`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", reading (a) for a lawyer; fork F33): "and if so whether the report"
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:5825 | (2) The company must not publish with non-statutory accounts the auditor's report on the company's statutory accounts.
@ref s 435(2) The company must not publish with non-statutory accounts the auditor's report on its statutory accounts (src:5825)
GIVEN `the company publishes non-statutory accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is the auditor's report on the company's statutory accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 435(2) the company is barred from publishing the auditor's report on its statutory accounts with the non-statutory accounts` MEANS
    IF `the company publishes non-statutory accounts` AND `the document is the auditor's report on the company's statutory accounts`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the bar: "The company must not publish with non-statutory accounts the auditor's report on the company's statutory accounts"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar names that one document published with non-statutory accounts

-- src:5826 | (3) References in this section to the publication by a company of “non-statutory accounts” are to the publication of—
-- src:5827 | (a) any balance sheet or profit and loss account relating to, or purporting to deal with, a financial year of the company, or
-- src:5828 | (b) an account in any form purporting to be a balance sheet or profit and loss account for a group headed by the company relating to, or purporting to deal with, a financial year of the company,
-- src:5829 | otherwise than as part of the company's statutory accounts.
@ref s 435(3) What is the publication of "non-statutory accounts" (src:5826-5829)
GIVEN `the document is a balance sheet or profit and loss account relating to, or purporting to deal with, a financial year of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is an account in any form purporting to be a balance sheet or profit and loss account for a group headed by the company relating to, or purporting to deal with, a financial year of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is published as part of the company's statutory accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 435(3) the publication is the publication of non-statutory accounts` MEANS
    IF (`the document is a balance sheet or profit and loss account relating to, or purporting to deal with, a financial year of the company`
        OR `the document is an account in any form purporting to be a balance sheet or profit and loss account for a group headed by the company relating to, or purporting to deal with, a financial year of the company`)
       AND NOT (`the document is published as part of the company's statutory accounts`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "References in this section to the publication by a company of “non-statutory accounts” are to the publication of— (a) ... or (b) ... otherwise than as part of the company's statutory accounts"

-- src:5830 | (4) In subsection (3)(b) “a group headed by the company” means a group consisting of the company and any other undertaking (regardless of whether it is a subsidiary undertaking of the company) other than a parent undertaking of the company.
@ref s 435(4) Meaning of "a group headed by the company" (src:5830)
GIVEN `the group consists of the company and any other undertaking (regardless of whether it is a subsidiary undertaking of the company)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the group includes a parent undertaking of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 435(4) the group is a group headed by the company` MEANS
    IF `the group consists of the company and any other undertaking (regardless of whether it is a subsidiary undertaking of the company)`
       AND NOT (`the group includes a parent undertaking of the company`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“a group headed by the company” means a group consisting of the company and any other undertaking ... other than a parent undertaking of the company"

-- src:5831 | (5) If a company contravenes any provision of this section, an offence is committed by—
-- src:5832 | (a) the company, and
-- src:5833 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 435(5) Offences by the company and by every officer in default (src:5831-5833)
GIVEN `the company contravenes a provision of section 435` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 435(5)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the company contravenes a provision of section 435`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", reading (a) for a lawyer): "If a company contravenes any provision of this section, an offence is committed by— (a) the company"

@ref s 435(5) (src:5831)
GIVEN `the company contravenes a provision of section 435` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 435(5)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company contravenes a provision of section 435`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", reading (a) for a lawyer): "If a company contravenes any provision of this section, an offence is committed by— ... (b) every officer of the company who is in default"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is decided by section 1121

-- src:5834 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 435(6) Penalty for an offence under section 435: level 3 (src:5834)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 435(6) the penalty for an offence under section 435` MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection provides only for liability on summary conviction

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 436: Meaning of "publication" in relation to accounts and reports
-- =========================================================================================================

§ `s 436 Meaning of "publication" in relation to accounts and reports`

@ref s 435(6) Penalty for an offence under section 435: level 3 (src:5834)
DECLARE `s 436(1) section for the purposes of which this section has effect` IS ONE OF
    `s 436(1) section 433 (name of signatory to be stated in published copies of accounts and reports)`
    `s 436(1) section 434 (requirements in connection with publication of statutory accounts)`
    `s 436(1) section 435 (requirements in connection with publication of non-statutory accounts)`
    `s 436(1) another section`

-- src:5836 | 436 Meaning of “publication” in relation to accounts and reports
-- src:5837 | (1) This section has effect for the purposes of—
-- src:5838 | section 433 (name of signatory to be stated in published copies of accounts and reports),
-- src:5839 | section 434 (requirements in connection with publication of statutory accounts), and
-- src:5840 | section 435 (requirements in connection with publication of non-statutory accounts).
@ref s 436(1) The section has effect for the purposes of sections 433, 434 and 435 (src:5836-5840)
GIVEN section IS A `s 436(1) section for the purposes of which this section has effect`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 436(1) this section has effect for the purposes of the section` MEANS
    CONSIDER section
    WHEN `s 436(1) another section` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection names three sections and is not followed by "only"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:5841 | (2) For the purposes of those sections a company is regarded as publishing a document if it publishes, issues or circulates it or otherwise makes it available for public inspection in a manner calculated to invite members of the public generally, or any class of members of the public, to read it.
@ref s 436(2) A company is regarded as publishing a document if it publishes, issues or circulates it or otherwise makes it available for public inspection in a manner calculated to invite the public to read it (src:5841)
GIVEN `the company publishes the document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company issues the document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company circulates the document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company otherwise makes the document available for public inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it does so in a manner calculated to invite members of the public generally, or any class of members of the public, to read it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 436(2) the company is regarded as publishing the document` MEANS
    IF (`the company publishes the document` OR `the company issues the document` OR `the company circulates the document` OR `the company otherwise makes the document available for public inspection`)
       AND `it does so in a manner calculated to invite members of the public generally, or any class of members of the public, to read it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", reading (a) for a lawyer; fork F27 on how far "in a manner calculated to invite" reaches): "a company is regarded as publishing a document if it publishes, issues or circulates it or otherwise makes it available for public inspection in a manner calculated to invite members of the public generally, or any class of members of the public, to read it"
